<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oria (Apulia)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oria is a hill town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brindisi">Brindisi</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. As ancient Uria it was one of the main centres of the Messapians, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> reports a tradition that it was founded by Cretans. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the seat of a learned Jewish community and of a bishopric, and its castle dates from the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>.</p></div>
